{"Title":"An Act relative to the Massachusetts estate tax","BillNumber":"S1816","DocketNumber":"SD2349","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"RCF0","Name":"Ryan C. Fattman","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RCF0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T16:40:53.367"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"RCF0","Name":"Ryan C. Fattman","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RCF0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T16:40:53.3666667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1816/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Fattman, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1816) of Ryan C. Fattman relative to the Massachusetts estate tax.  Revenue.","DocumentText":"\tSection 2A of chapter 65C of the general laws, as appearing in the 2020 edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the word “commonwealth”, in line 3, the following words:- ; provided, however, that no tax shall be imposed on the transfer of an estate valued at or less than $5,000,000. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}